apers**. The table is cluttered with papers, books, and what appear to be official forms or ledgers. The standing figure is seen gesturing towards and handling these documents, indicating that decisions, orders, or judgments are being made based on the written information.\n\n- **Official Documents:** The papers on the table are likely official records, petitions, decrees, or legal documents. The characters are not using modern technology or digital means; instead, they rely on traditional, physical paperwork, which aligns with the medieval or fantastical setting.\n- **Oral Communication:** While the documents are central, there is also an element of oral communication. The standing figure appears to be speaking or giving instructions, and the seated figures are listening attentively. This suggests a combination of written and verbal communication, typical of formal administrative or judicial proceedings.\n- **No Scrolls or Digital Media:** There is no evidence of scrolls, tablets, or any form of digital media. The communication is entirely analog, relying on paper and direct verbal interaction.\n\n**Interaction Between Officials and Citizens:**\nThe scene depicts a formal interaction between an authority figure and several other characters. The standing official appears to be presiding over a meeting or hearing, while the seated figures are either presenting their cases or receiving instructions. The presence of multiple documents and the focused attention of all participants suggest that this is a serious, official proceeding, possibly involving legal, administrative, or bureaucratic matters.\n\nIn summary, the communication in these frames is primarily through **written documents and oral discourse** in a formal, hierarchical setting. The method of information exchange is traditional and official, fitting the dark, mystical, and medieval-inspired world of the video. There is no indication of modern or digital communication methods, reinforcing the fantastical and historical tone of the narrative.'}], 'formatted_responses': ['\n=== Batch 0-13 (13 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2sriHX3PbXw/frames/frame_1602.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2sriHX3PbXw/frames/frame_1606.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2sriHX3PbXw/frames/frame_1607.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2sriHX3PbXw/frames/frame_1608.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2sriHX3PbXw/frames/frame_1609.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2sriHX3PbXw/frames/frame_1613.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2sriHX3PbXw/frames/frame_1618.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2sriHX3PbXw/frames/frame_1624.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2sriHX3PbXw/frames/frame_1627.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2sriHX3PbXw/frames/frame_1628.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2sriHX3PbXw/frames/frame_1633.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2sriHX3PbXw/frames/frame_1638.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2sriHX3PbXw/frames/frame_1639.jpg\nVLM Response: Based on the provided frames and the global summary, here is an analysis of communication and information exchange in these specific scenes:\n\n**Setting:**\nThe scene is set in a dimly lit, formal room, likely an office, study, or council chamber within a larger, possibly medieval or gothic-style building. The presence of large, ornate windows and a long, heavy table suggests an official or administrative space. The atmosphere is somber and serious, consistent with the overall dark and mystical vibe of the video.\n\n**Characters and Roles:**\nThe scene features several puppet or stop-motion characters gathered around a large table. One figure, standing at the head of the table and appearing to address the others, seems to be in a position of authority—perhaps a government official, a judge, or a high-ranking bureaucrat. The other figures seated around the table appear to be subordinates, clerks, or citizens petitioning the official. Their postures and the way they are focused on the documents suggest a formal, hierarchical interaction.\n\n**Method of Information Exchange:**\nThe primary method of communication and information exchange in this scene is **through written documents and papers**. The table is cluttered with papers, books, and what appear to be official forms or ledgers. The standing figure is seen gesturing towards and handling these documents, indicating that decisions, orders, or judgments are being made based on the written information.\n\n- **Official Documents:** The papers on the table are likely official records, petitions, decrees, or legal documents. The characters are not using modern technology or digital means; instead, they rely on traditional, physical paperwork, which aligns with the medieval or fantastical setting.\n- **Oral Communication:** While the documents are central, there is also an element of oral communication. The standing figure appears to be speaking or giving instructions, and the seated figures are listening attentively. This suggests a combination of written and verbal communication, typical of formal administrative or judicial proceedings.\n- **No Scrolls or Digital Media:** There is no evidence of scrolls, tablets, or any form of digital media. The communication is entirely analog, relying on paper and direct verbal interaction.\n\n**Interaction Between Officials and Citizens:**\nThe scene depicts a formal interaction between an authority figure and several other characters. The standing official appears to be presiding over a meeting or hearing, while the seated figures are either presenting their cases or receiving instructions. The presence of multiple documents and the focused attention of all participants suggest that this is a serious, official proceeding, possibly involving legal, administrative, or bureaucratic matters.\n\nIn summary, the communication in these frames is primarily through **written documents an